{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/a2-october-days-halloween-canadian-thanksgiving-german-unity-day/audio/main-de1c807c13cc.mp3","durationSec":206.448,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":1.36,"text":"Halloween is on 31 October."},{"start":3.28,"end":8.4,"text":"In the United States, Canada, the United Kingdom, and Ireland, people wear costumes."},{"start":9.22,"end":14.64,"text":"A costume is clothing that makes someone look like another person or thing, such as a witch or a ghost."},{"start":15.8,"end":17.22,"text":"Children go from door to door."},{"start":17.82,"end":20.68,"text":"At each door, they say “Trick or treat!”"},{"start":20.68,"end":22.72,"text":"Neighbours give them candy."},{"start":23.36,"end":26.74,"text":"This activity is called trick-or-treat."},{"start":26.74,"end":29.06,"text":"Children often carry a bag for their candy."},{"start":29.56,"end":33.44,"text":"A parent or another adult often walks with young children."},{"start":34.6,"end":37.56,"text":"Some Halloween costumes are scary, and some are funny."},{"start":38.3,"end":41.96,"text":"One person can dress as a ghost, and a friend can dress as a big banana."},{"start":41.96,"end":44.28,"text":"Adults wear costumes too."},{"start":45.36,"end":49.24,"text":"Many go to costume parties, where people meet friends in their costumes."},{"start":50.06,"end":53.46,"text":"People also cut pumpkins into jack-o-lanterns."},{"start":53.46,"end":56.58,"text":"They take out the inside of a pumpkin and cut a face into it."},{"start":56.58,"end":60.4,"text":"A light inside the pumpkin makes the face shine in the dark."},{"start":60.4,"end":65.18,"text":"Canadian Thanksgiving is the second Monday of October."},{"start":65.74,"end":68.68,"text":"In 2026, that Monday is 12 October."},{"start":68.68,"end":76.12,"text":"1 October is a Thursday, so 5 October is the first Monday and 12 October is the second Monday."},{"start":76.12,"end":80.74,"text":"Families sit down for a harvest meal, often on the Sunday or the Monday."},{"start":81.5,"end":83.18,"text":"Roast turkey is a common main dish."},{"start":83.18,"end":87.46,"text":"Families often serve it with stuffing, potatoes, and cranberry sauce."},{"start":88.46,"end":90.28,"text":"Stuffing is a mixture often made with bread."},{"start":90.28,"end":92.84,"text":"Pumpkin pie comes after the main meal."},{"start":93.42,"end":95.6,"text":"People give thanks for the harvest and the year."},{"start":100.88,"end":105.82,"text":"Since 1957, Canadian Thanksgiving has been on the second Monday of October."},{"start":106.58,"end":112.68,"text":"In 2026, the long weekend runs from Saturday 10 October to Monday 12 October."},{"start":113.32,"end":116.94,"text":"A long weekend gives many people three days away from school or work."},{"start":117.7,"end":120.82,"text":"Many people travel home to see family and share the harvest meal."},{"start":121.8,"end":127.38,"text":"Thanksgiving is a day off in most of Canada, so schools, banks, and many workplaces close."},{"start":128.3,"end":131.56,"text":"In French, the day is called Action de grâce."},{"start":131.56,"end":134.3,"text":"People often say “Happy Thanksgiving” to family and friends."},{"start":135,"end":138.56,"text":"People in the United States keep Thanksgiving on the fourth Thursday of November."},{"start":139.34,"end":140.98,"text":"German Unity Day is on 3 October."},{"start":141.62,"end":144.86,"text":"Its German name is Tag der Deutschen Einheit."},{"start":145.36,"end":146.88,"text":"It is Germany’s national day."},{"start":147.56,"end":150.38,"text":"Germany was once East Germany and West Germany."},{"start":150.94,"end":155.74,"text":"Their official names were the German Democratic Republic and the Federal Republic of Germany."},{"start":157,"end":159.92,"text":"The Berlin Wall divided East and West Berlin."},{"start":160.62,"end":164.68,"text":"After protests, the Berlin Wall opened on 9 November 1989."},{"start":165.76,"end":169.3,"text":"On 3 October 1990, East Germany joined West Germany."},{"start":169.86,"end":172.34,"text":"This joining is called reunification."},{"start":173.74,"end":177.18,"text":"German Unity Day is a public holiday, so people have the day off."},{"start":177.82,"end":179.58,"text":"Many towns hold public gatherings."},{"start":180.56,"end":183.64,"text":"Each year, one German state hosts the main celebration."},{"start":184.46,"end":186.84,"text":"In 2026, that state is Bremen."},{"start":187.54,"end":192.04,"text":"Its city-centre festival runs from 2 to 4 October, and it is free to enter."},{"start":192.64,"end":196.4,"text":"People can hear concerts and talks across the city centre."},{"start":196.4,"end":200.92,"text":"Berlin also has events near the Brandenburg Gate, a famous landmark in the city."},{"start":201.36,"end":206.02,"text":"People see black, red, and gold flags and hear speeches about the country and its history."}],"words":[{"text":"Halloween","start":0,"end":0.5},{"text":"is","start":0.5,"end":0.82},{"text":"on","start":0.82,"end":0.98},{"text":"31","start":0.98,"end":0.99},{"text":"October","start":0.98,"end":1.36},{"text":"In","start":3.28,"end":3.32},{"text":"the","start":3.32,"end":3.42},{"text":"United","start":3.42,"end":3.68},{"text":"States","start":3.68,"end":4.24},{"text":"Canada","start":4.64,"end":4.86},{"text":"the","start":5.32,"end":5.38},{"text":"United","start":5.38,"end":5.66},{"text":"Kingdom","start":5.66,"end":6.1},{"text":"and","start":6.38,"end":6.48},{"text":"Ireland","start":6.48,"end":6.9},{"text":"people","start":7.46,"end":7.62},{"text":"wear","start":7.62,"end":7.86},{"text":"costumes","start":7.86,"end":8.4},{"text":"A","start":9.22,"end":9.32},{"text":"costume","start":9.32,"end":9.68},{"text":"is","start":9.68,"end":10},{"text":"clothing","start":10,"end":10.36},{"text":"that","start":10.36,"end":10.58},{"text":"makes","start":10.58,"end":10.84},{"text":"someone","start":10.84,"end":11.28},{"text":"look","start":11.28,"